    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0341" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4082: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-27T12:00:00-06:00">July 27,
                            1943—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 28—4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>748. Department’s 1185, July 24. With minimum 2 months’ notice 500 to 1,000
                    additional refugees could be accomplished [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >accommodated?</hi>] in Colonia Santa Rosa.</p>
                <p>For additional large groups it would be necessary to establish new centers and we
                    would require 5 to 6 months’ advance notification.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
